  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 230 PM CDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nThursday-Friday:\nConvection will likely be ongoing into Thursday morning, with\nthe best coverage confined to portions of central MO. Activity\ngradually dissipates through Thursday morning, with low\nconfidence in any redevelopment along the front into Thursday\nafternoon as the better lift becomes displaced. For now, rain \nchances are around 10-30%. However, SPC introduced another \nMarginal (1 of 5) risk for isolated strong to severe \nthunderstorms on Thursday. This is supported by the lingering \ninstability and deep layer shear. Otherwise, a wide variance of \nhigh temperatures on Thursday ranging from middle 80s (north) to\nmiddle 90s (south).\n\nBy Thursday night, additional shortwave energy is progged to\nmove into the area with a nocturnal low-level jet in place. The\nhighest shower and thunderstorm chances Thursday night into\nFriday morning will focused along the frontal boundary placement\nonce again, and thus there may be the need to expand the Flood\nWatch. This lingering uncertainty will be better analyzed in\nsubsequent forecast updates over the next 24 hours. Likewise, we\nwill need to closely monitor the potential for marginally severe\nthunderstorms and/or localized heavy rainfall and flash\nflooding. The front gradually slides south and east of the\nregion through Friday.\n\nThis Weekend-Early Next Week:\nAs we get beyond Friday, an upper-level ridge gradually returns\nto the region. This would support a return of hot and humid\nconditions, in addition to drier weather. Highs on Saturday and\nSunday reach back into the middle 90s, with heat index values\naround 100 to 105. This remains the storyline heading into early\nnext week. While this heat is fairly common for this time of the\nyear, we will still need to monitor for potential heat \nheadlines. It is worth noting, the area remains on the eastern \nperiphery of the ridge, with subtle differences or shifts in the\npattern potentially reintroducing some thunderstorm chances \ninto our area early next week.",
